1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,160
Narrator: Scenario 23. Network and access.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:16,080
B: The customer search page takes almost two seconds from our US office. Our Singapore colleague sees the same page load in about half a second.

3
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:26,208
A: Let us compare the same request type and time window. Different search terms or cached responses could make the regional comparison misleading.

4
00:00:26,808 --> 00:00:39,408
C: Please collect request IDs, UTC timestamps, and source locations. I can combine the application traces with approved network measurements from both locations.

5
00:00:40,008 --> 00:00:49,800
B: I have ten requests using the same test account and search terms. The browser timings show most of the delay before the first response byte.

6
00:00:50,400 --> 00:01:02,352
A: That includes network time and server processing. The matching traces show similar processing times, around 180 milliseconds, so we should inspect the connection path.

7
00:01:02,952 --> 00:01:15,264
C: The US office traffic crosses the corporate inspection proxy before reaching Asia. A direct approved monitoring probe has substantially lower connection establishment time.

8
00:01:15,864 --> 00:01:25,656
B: Does that mean we should remove the proxy for everyone? Sales is asking whether customers outside the office are experiencing the same slowdown.

9
00:01:26,256 --> 00:01:37,200
A: We do not have evidence of broad customer impact yet. External probes remain near baseline, and changing the proxy path requires a separate review.

10
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:47,832
C: I found elevated connection queue time on the US proxy pool. I will check its capacity and recent policy changes with the network owner.

11
00:01:48,432 --> 00:01:59,256
A: Please preserve those measurements before any adjustment. We can repeat the ten-request comparison afterward and verify that the inspection controls still function.

12
00:01:59,856 --> 00:02:11,424
B: I will coordinate the office retest at 16:00 UTC and ask support for any matching customer reports, including timestamps and affected locations.

13
00:02:12,024 --> 00:02:22,272
A: At that checkpoint, we will share the measured impact and next action. We should describe the proxy evidence without declaring a root cause prematurely.
